{"schema":1,"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.AdditiveValuationNorms.ShaLeV:7:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.PropA.shaLeV","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/AdditiveValuationNorms/ShaLeV.lean","lines":[7,16],"atlasRow":385728,"chapter":"1.5992","archiveCommit":"40e56bab026552e089d7afcfeff08d2defb9c005","provenance":{"fileSha256":"bf65172b1182f9d50858d61ad23b75e9c2755963a01b90cd9aff14aa3f8f575b","commandSha256":"16dba7d334cc158448ffcbbd845343add8ebd09f95d21bae1712a85e0569ba48"},"source":["theorem UpperTheory.V.PropA.shaLeV :","    GlobalTheory.Published.PoitouTateDuality → LocalFinitenessK → LocalTateDualityK →","      ∀ (F Ω : Type) [Field F] [NumberField F] [Field Ω] [Algebra F Ω] [IsAlgClosure F Ω] (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime],","        PTCase F l → ∀ (D : LData F Ω l) (e : ℤ), shaLen D e ≤ VLen D e := by","  intro hPT hLF hLT F Ω _ _ _ _ _ l _ hc D e","  have hfl := fun r hr => GlobalTheory.TateLimit.finite_level D e hPT hc r hr","  have hsa : PTShaAt D e := GlobalTheory.TateLimit.ptShaAt D e hLF hLT (fun r hr => (hfl r hr).1)","    (fun r hr => (hfl r hr).2.1) (hfl 1 one_pos).2.2","  rw [VLen, ← hsa hc]","  exact Module.length_le_of_injective (f := (Sha2Zl D e).subtype) (hf := Subtype.val_injective)"],"statementLines":[7,10],"proofLines":[10,16],"assume":["Assume `GlobalTheory.Published.PoitouTateDuality` (hPT).","Assume `LocalFinitenessK` (hLF).","Assume `LocalTateDualityK` (hLT).","Assume `PTCase F l` (hc)."],"show":"Assume global Poitou–Tate duality, local finiteness and local Tate duality. For a number field F with an algebraic closure, a prime ℓ satisfying the required Poitou–Tate case, any allowed local data D and integer twist e, the first locally trivial cohomology length is at most the indicated second cohomology length.","strategy":"Assemble the finite-level duality isomorphisms and the local inputs into the length identity for the second locally trivial group. That group is a submodule of the second cohomology group.","steps":[{"id":"g-10-76","number":"⟨1⟩1","kind":"have","claim":"At each $r>0$, global Poitou–Tate duality supplies the finite-level cohomological duality data for $D$ and the twist $e$ with coefficients of exponent $\\ell^r$. Its case hypothesis holds for odd $\\ell$ and requires $F$ to have no real places at $\\ell=2$.","lines":[10,12],"headLines":[10,12],"snippet":"        PTCase F l → ∀ (D : LData F Ω l) (e : ℤ), shaLen D e ≤ VLen D e := by\n  intro hPT hLF hLT F Ω _ _ _ _ _ l _ hc D e\n  have hfl := fun r hr => GlobalTheory.TateLimit.finite_level D e hPT hc r hr","uses":[{"id":"Development.AbelianVarietyTheory.Proofs.FoundationProofs.LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels:517:9","name":"GlobalTheory.TateLimit.finite_level","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AbelianVarietyTheory/Proofs/FoundationProofs/LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels.lean","lines":[517,525],"atlasRow":232762,"owner":"1.3616"}],"refs":[],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":false,"children":[]},{"id":"g-13-3","number":"⟨1⟩2","kind":"have","claim":"The passage to the limit uses the finite-level comparisons at each $r>0$, their level-one specialization, local finiteness, and local Tate duality. It equates the $\\mathbf Z_\\ell$-length of the degree-two integral localization kernel at twist $e+1$ with the length of the degree-one kernel for $(\\mathbf Q_\\ell/\\mathbf Z_\\ell)(-e)$. On these latter coefficients the Galois action is multiplication by $\\chi^{-e}$.","lines":[13,14],"headLines":[13,14],"snippet":"  have hsa : PTShaAt D e := GlobalTheory.TateLimit.ptShaAt D e hLF hLT (fun r hr => (hfl r hr).1)\n    (fun r hr => (hfl r hr).2.1) (hfl 1 one_pos).2.2","uses":[{"id":"Development.AbelianVarietyTheory.Proofs.FoundationProofs.LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels:462:9","name":"GlobalTheory.TateLimit.ptShaAt","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AbelianVarietyTheory/Proofs/FoundationProofs/LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels.lean","lines":[462,513],"atlasRow":232761,"owner":"1.3499"},{"id":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.Statement:101:5","name":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.PTShaAt","kind":"def","file":"Formalism/GaloisCohomology/Statement.lean","lines":[101,102],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.10568"}],"refs":[],"typedFact":"PTShaAt D e","secondRead":false,"children":[]},{"id":"g-15-3","number":"⟨1⟩3","kind":"rewrite","claim":"The degree-one kernel has the same length as the degree-two integral localization kernel. The latter is a submodule of $H^2(G_S,\\mathbf Z_\\ell(e+1))$, so its injective inclusion gives the claimed upper bound by the length of this entire cohomology group, also in the extended naturals.","lines":[15,16],"headLines":[15,16],"snippet":"  rw [VLen, ← hsa hc]\n  exact Module.length_le_of_injective (f := (Sha2Zl D e).subtype) (hf := Subtype.val_injective)","uses":[{"id":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.Statement:80:5","name":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.VLen","kind":"def","file":"Formalism/GaloisCohomology/Statement.lean","lines":[80,80],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.10568"},{"id":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.Statement:82:5","name":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.Sha2Zl","kind":"def","file":"Formalism/GaloisCohomology/Statement.lean","lines":[82,83],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.10568"}],"refs":["g-13-3"],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":false,"children":[]}],"uses":[{"id":"Development.AbelianVarietyTheory.Proofs.FoundationProofs.LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels:165:5","name":"GlobalTheory.TateLimit.redChar","kind":"def","file":"Development/AbelianVarietyTheory/Proofs/FoundationProofs/LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels.lean","lines":[165,166],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.3603"},{"id":"Development.AbelianVarietyTheory.Proofs.FoundationProofs.LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels:251:8","name":"GlobalTheory.TateLimit.zr","kind":"abbrev","file":"Development/AbelianVarietyTheory/Proofs/FoundationProofs/LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels.lean","lines":[251,253],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.3616"},{"id":"Development.AbelianVarietyTheory.Proofs.FoundationProofs.LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels:255:9","name":"GlobalTheory.TateLimit.contAction_zr","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AbelianVarietyTheory/Proofs/FoundationProofs/LengthEqLengthInvariantsOfTorsionLevels.lean","lines":[255,257],"atlasRow":232746,"owner":"1.3616"},{"id":"Development.AbelianVarietyTheory.PublishedTheorems.GaloisCohomology₂.ExistsPrimitiveRootPow:13:5","name":"GlobalTheory.Published.PoitouTateDuality","kind":"def","file":"Development/AbelianVarietyTheory/PublishedTheorems/GaloisCohomology₂/ExistsPrimitiveRootPow.lean","lines":[13,27],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.5870"},{"id":"Development.AbelianVarietyTheory.PublishedTheorems.GaloisCohomology₂.PoitouTateNineTermTransgressionZeroApply:150:5","name":"GlobalTheory.Published.PoitouTate.NineTermExact","kind":"def","file":"Development/AbelianVarietyTheory/PublishedTheorems/GaloisCohomology₂/PoitouTateNineTermTransgressionZeroApply.lean","lines":[150,161],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.5870"},{"id":"Development.AbelianVarietyTheory.PublishedTheorems.GaloisCohomology₂.PoitouTateNineTermTransgressionZeroApply:163:5","name":"GlobalTheory.Published.PoitouTate.ShaDual","kind":"def","file":"Development/AbelianVarietyTheory/PublishedTheorems/GaloisCohomology₂/PoitouTateNineTermTransgressionZeroApply.lean","lines":[163,175],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.5870"},{"id":"Formalism.ConjugateSelfDual.Statement:6:8","name":"Formalism.ConjugateSelfDual.G","kind":"abbrev","file":"Formalism/ConjugateSelfDual/Statement.lean","lines":[6,6],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.10481"},{"id":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.LocalTateDualityK:41:5","name":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.LocalFinitenessK","kind":"def","file":"Formalism/GaloisCohomology/LocalTateDualityK.lean","lines":[41,45],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.10568"},{"id":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.LocalTateDualityK:47:5","name":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.LocalTateDualityK","kind":"def","file":"Formalism/GaloisCohomology/LocalTateDualityK.lean","l